.TH PAPIRO 1 "October 2026" "Papiro 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Papiro \- A focused, cross-platform text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B papiro
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Papiro
is a modern, cross-platform text editor designed for developers and writers who value focus and efficiency. It provides syntax highlighting for 10+ programming languages, multiple cursors and selections, macro recording and playback, a clip library for snippets, spell checking via Hunspell, dark/light themes, and translations for Portuguese, English, and Spanish.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-new
Create a new document.
.TP
.BI \-\-open=FILE
Open the specified file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/Papiro/Papiro.conf
Main configuration file (QSettings).
.TP
.I ~/.config/Papiro/cliplib.json
Clip library data.
.TP
.I ~/.config/Papiro/macros/
Macro files and slot assignments.
.TP
.I ~/.config/Papiro/tools.json
External tools configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt platform plugin (e.g., xcb, wayland, offscreen).
.TP
.I LANG
Interface language (pt, en, es).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open a file:
.B papiro main.cpp
.TP
Open multiple files:
.B papiro file1.py file2.py file3.py
